    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The basic parabola"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The graph of $y = x^2$ is a U-shaped curve called a **parabola**. It is symmetrical about the $y$-axis, and its lowest point, the **turning point**, is at the origin $(0; 0)$."
    },
