    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Finding the equation"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 2",
      "problem": "A parabola of the form $y = ax^2 + q$ has a turning point at $(0; -3)$ and passes through $(2; 5)$. Find its equation.",
      "steps": [
        "Turning point $(0; -3)$ gives $q = -3$: $y = ax^2 - 3$.",
        "Substitute $(2; 5)$: $5 = a(4) - 3$, so $4a = 8$ and $a = 2$.",
        "$y = 2x^2 - 3$"
      ],
      "answer": "$y = 2x^2 - 3$"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "label": "Exam tip",
      "text": "When you sketch a graph, always label the turning point, the intercepts with the axes and the graph itself. A sketch does not need to be on graph paper, but it must have the correct shape and position."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Reading from graphs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If $f$ and $g$ are drawn on the same axes, then $f(x) = g(x)$ where the graphs **intersect**, and $f(x) > g(x)$ where the graph of $f$ lies **above** the graph of $g$."
    }
  ],
